[[Example only. Characters, places and lines are placeholders made up for this template, not part of the story.]]

FADE IN:

INT. FIELD COMMAND TENT - DAWN

[[AMBIENCE: rain on canvas, distant engines]]
[[MUSIC: low drums, tense]]

A folding table, a paper map pinned down with a helmet. MAJOR HALVERSEN, fifties, leans over it. LIEUTENANT ODA stands by the radio.

MAJOR HALVERSEN
(tired, steady)
Commander. They're coming for the river, and they're coming today.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: two arrows from the north towards BRIDGE_WEST and BRIDGE_EAST]]

MAJOR HALVERSEN
Two bridges. We can't hold both. The engineers can drop the west one, but they need twelve minutes and nobody shooting at them.

LIEUTENANT ODA
(sharp)
Scouts report armour on the north road. Lots of it.

[[SFX: radio static]]

MAJOR HALVERSEN
Then you give the engineers their twelve minutes. Keep the post standing until that bridge goes into the water. After that, nothing crosses in the east.

[[SFX: distant explosion]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
